  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 300 AM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nSaturday-Thursday:\nFriday's system dissipates to the south and east into Saturday\nmorning, with isolated showers and thunderstorm chances (10-30%)\nlingering through the morning. The timing of dissipation will\nplay a role in how quickly heat and humidity are able to\noverspread the area. This approaching heat wave is characterized\nby a strong upper level ridge building into the region. 850mb\ntemperatures are progged to push 23 to 25 C as early as Saturday\nacross the western half of the area. If clouds and precipitation\nclear the area by Saturday afternoon, temperatures look to push\ninto the lower to upper 90s. Confidence in this potential is\ngreatest along and west of Highway 65 on Saturday afternoon,\nwith heat index values approaching 100 to 110. This is well\nsupported by the probabilistic suite of guidance. There is \nstill a bit of uncertainty on the extent of dewpoints actually \nreaching into the upper 70s, but the message remains consistent \nfor excessive heat. For this reason, an Extreme Heat Watch has \nbeen issued for the entire area from 1pm Saturday through 7pm \nTuesday. \n\nConfidence increases into Sunday, and beyond into early next\nweek that a heat wave takes shape over the region. High\ntemperatures soar well into the middle to upper 90s, with low\n100s across southeast KS and southwest MO. This will be\naccompanied by heat index values ranging from 100 to 110+. Thus,\nconfidence in heat headlines is high, and is a matter of\nadvisory versus warning criteria being met. A few record highs\nmay be approached, as seen in the Climate section of the AFD.\nMinimal overnight relief is expected with this heat wave, with\novernight lows staying in the upper 70s to near 80. The hottest\ntemperatures occur on Sunday through Tuesday. Any necessary \nplans should be put into action, allowing ample time to prepare \nfor a prolonged, multiple day heat wave.\n\nMeanwhile, any precipitation chances remain minimal beyond\nSaturday, at less than 10%. While confidence is highest in the\nheat wave persisting into Tuesday, there is some indications\nthat the heat lingers into the middle of next week. This will be\ndetermined by if the upper level ridge retrieves back to the \neast or remains stationed over the region.",
